More specifically it's negative-sum. NFT value and backing cancel at settlement. Protocol creates nothing. Just moves assets and takes a cut. Buyers need V/B above 1.10. Depositors need below 1.07. No overlap. Both sides lose in the gap. Emissions hid it for 15 days. Those ended.

Also worth remembering: v1 was drained via Chainlink callback front-run. And the "permissionless" collection whitelist is owner-curated the burn-to-enter path launched disabled on mainnet. Attacker took CryptoPunk #5450 for roughly $66k in ETH and protocol was paused and patched.

